      \"resolved_references\": 80,\n      \"total_references\": 176\n    },\n    \"verification_report_path\": \"work/results/t02/codex/20261112_215258/paper/scientific-evidence/verification-report.json\"\n  },\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-13T04:48:34.346391+00:00\",\n  \"hard_errors\": [\n    \"agentic evidence audit failed: see work/results/t02/codex/20261112_215258/paper/paper_evidence_audit_feedback.json and work/results/t02/codex/20261112_215258/paper/paper_evidence_audit.md\",\n    \"figure validation failed: figures[1] figure_type does not match strategy for width_endpoint_comparison; figures[2] figure_type does not match strategy for fit_and_generalization_onsets\"\n  ],\n  \"ok\": false,\n  \"page_validation\": {\n    \"body_pages\": null,\n    \"checked\": false,\n    \"errors\": [],\n    \"exclude_references\": false,\n    \"last_body_page_counted\": null,\n    \"last_body_page_fill_ratio\": null,\n    \"last_body_page_number\": null,\n    \"max_body_pages\": null,\n    \"min_body_pages\": null,\n    \"min_last_body_page_fill_ratio\": null,\n    \"paper_format\": null,\n    \"reference_start_page\": null,\n    \"supplement_pages\": 0,\n    \"supplement_start_page\": null,\n    \"total_pages\": null\n  },\n  \"paper_dir\": \"work/results/t02/codex/20261112_215258/paper\",\n  \"pdf_path\": null,\n  \"soft_warnings\": [\n    \"figures[0] PNG height too small: 600 < 700\",\n    \"figures[1] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\",\n    \"figures[2] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\"\n  ],\n  \"supplementary_information_validation\": {\n    \"appendix_present\": true,\n    \"checked\": true,\n    \"clearpage_present\": true,\n    \"errors\": [],\n    \"heading_present\": true,\n    \"placed_after_references\": true,\n    \"pre_bibliography_clearpage_present\": true,\n    \"rendered_checked\": false,\n    \"rendered_heading_present\": false,\n    \"rendered_visible_character_count\": 0,\n    \"substantive_element_count\": 7,\n    \"visible_character_count\": 9800\n  }\n}# Paper validation feedback\n\n- generated_at: 2026-11-13T04:48:34.346391+00:00\n- paper_dir: `work/results/t02/codex/20261112_215258/paper`\n- ok: `False`\n\n## Hard errors\n- agentic evidence audit failed: see work/results/t02/codex/20261112_215258/paper/paper_evidence_audit_feedback.json and work/results/t02/codex/20261112_215258/paper/paper_evidence_audit.md\n- figure validation failed: figures[1] figure_type does not match strategy for width_endpoint_comparison; figures[2] figure_type does not match strategy for fit_and_generalization_onsets\n\n## Supplementary Information validation\n- appendix_present: `True`\n- heading_present: `True`\n- placed_after_references: `True`\n- pre_bibliography_clearpage_present: `True`\n- clearpage_present: `True`\n- visible_character_count: `9800`\n- substantive_element_count: `7`\n- rendered_checked: `False`\n- rendered_heading_present: `False`\n- rendered_visible_character_count: `0`\n\n## Evidence validation\n- bundle_path: `work/results/t02/codex/20261112_215258/paper/scientific-evidence`\n- bundle_present: `True`\n- verification_report: `work/results/t02/codex/20261112_215258/paper/scientific-evidence/verification-report.json`\n- total_references: `176`\n- resolved_references: `80`\n- anchored_references: `96`\n- dangling_references: `0`\n- manifests_checked: `14`\n\n## Agentic evidence audit\n- checked: `True`\n- verdict: `fail`\n- finding_count: `1`\n- summary: Numerical results and qualification limitations are grounded, but the manuscript describes a completed overview figure that remains an unrendered placeholder.\n\n### Audit findings to fix\n- `overview-rendering-1` (Introduction Figure 1; Supplementary Information—Reproducibility): The included image contains only a pending-rendering message; the rendering workflow failed, contradicting the manuscript’s completed-rendering claim and figure description.\n  - claim: The overview depicts the study design and “is rendered separately by the designated concept-figure workflow.”\n  - evidence: paper.tex:51 and paper.tex:52 include and describe figures/study_overview.png; paper.tex:361 asserts rendering; the PNG reads “Concept overview pending orchestrator rendering”; figure_manifest.json records generator=null, rendering exit code 1, and a placeholder note.\n  - requested_fix: Remove the placeholder figure and its descriptive caption, and remove or qualify the supplementary claim that rendering completed; retain the supported study-design explanation in prose.\n\n## Soft warnings\n- figures[0] PNG height too small: 600 < 700\n- figures[1] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\n- figures[2] PNG width too small: 1650 < 2400\n{\n  \"audit_json_path\": \"work/results/t02/codex/20261112_215258/paper/paper_evidence_audit.json\",\n  \"audit_markdown_path\": \"work/results/t02/codex/20261112_215258/paper/paper_evidence_audit.md\",\n  \"finding_count\": 1,\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"claim\": \"The overview depicts the study design and \\u201cis rendered separately by the designated concept-figure workflow.\\u201d\",\n      \"evidence\": \"paper.tex:51 and paper.tex:52 include and describe figures/study_overview.png; paper.tex:361 asserts rendering; the PNG reads \\u201cConcept overview pending orchestrator rendering\\u201d; figure_manifest.json records generator=null, rendering exit code 1, and a placeholder note.\",\n      \"fix\": \"Remove the placeholder figure and its descriptive caption, and remove or qualify the supplementary claim that rendering completed; retain the supported study-design explanation in prose.\",\n      \"id\": \"overview-rendering-1\",\n      \"issue\": \"The included image contains only a pending-rendering message; the rendering workflow failed, contradicting the manuscript\\u2019s completed-rendering claim and figure description.\",\n      \"section\": \"Introduction Figure 1; Supplementary Information\\u2014Reproducibility\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"generated_at\": \"2026-11-13T04:48:34.223112+00:00\",\n  \"ok\": false,\n  \"raw_output_path\": \"work/results/t02/codex/20261112_215258/paper/paper_evidence_audit_raw.txt\",\n  \"summary\": \"Numerical results and qualification limitations are grounded, but the manuscript describes a completed overview figure that remains an unrendered placeholder.\",\n  \"verdict\": \"fail\"\n}---\nname: validate-paper\ndescription: Validate grounded paper artifacts and compile LaTeX PDF with strict fail-fast checks.\n---\n\n# What the skill is about\nRun final quality gate for the generated paper.\n\n# When to use the skill\n- After `paper.tex`, `references.bib`, and `claims_grounding.json` are written.\n- Before declaring final paper success.\n\n# What to do\n1. Validate sections and citation keys:\n```bash\npython scripts/validate_tex_refs.py \\\n  --tex paper.tex \\\n  --bib references.bib\n```\nRequire a substantive embedded Supplementary Information section after the bibliography. It must\nuse `\\\\appendix` and `\\\\section{Supplementary Information}`, contain grounded visible content plus\nat least one subsection, table, or figure, and contain no template placeholder text.\n2. Validate claim mappings, bibliography/provenance consistency, and every `@evidence[[...]]` link in the `scientific-evidence/` bundle:\n```bash\npython ../write-paper/scripts/validate_claims.py \\\n  --paper-data paper_data.json \\\n  --references references_provenance.json \\\n  --bib references.bib \\\n  --claims claims_grounding.json \\\n  --paper-dir .\n```\nThis delegates to the `scientific-evidence` skill verifier, which classifies every `@evidence[[...]]` link as `resolved`, `anchored`, or `dangling`. Any `dangling` link (or an `@evidence[[...]]` token with no `scientific-evidence/` bundle present) is a hard error and must be sent back to the paper-writing agent for repair.\n3. Validate figure manifest and figure readability budget when `figure_manifest.json` is present or `paper_strategy.json` requires figures. The canonical schema is `templates/figure_manifest.schema.json`.\n```bash\npython .claude/skills/validate-paper/scripts/validate_figures.py \\\n  --paper-dir .\n```\n4. Compile:\n```bash\nbash scripts/compile_latex.sh paper.tex\n```\nThe compile script also validates that Supplementary Information is visibly rendered on a page\nafter References with substantive content. Source-only structure checks are not sufficient for\nconditional or literal LaTeX constructs.\nIt records and validates every LaTeX input, restricts BibTeX to the canonical `references.bib`,\nand removes inherited Kpathsea path overrides before compiling.\n5. Require `paper.pdf` to exist.\n6. When `paper_data.json.paper_profile == \"standalone\"`, also fail on visible paper language that leaks pipeline terms such as `eligible`, `correct and eligible`, `correctness rate`, `worker_01`, `worker_02`, `combined_score`, or similar internal wording.\n7. When the selected format or venue guidance requires real author metadata, also fail on anonymous or generic placeholder author blocks and emit soft warnings when title/abstract/introduction/conclusion lack venue-relevant framing or when the discussion drifts into unrelated application narratives.\n8. Fail hard on any missing grounding link, missing section, missing/empty/misordered Supplementary Information, unresolved citation, bibliography/provenance mismatch, figure-manifest mismatch, density-budget violation, page-limit violation for formats with enforced budgets, standalone-language violation, author-block violation required by format/venue guidance, dangling `@evidence[[...]]` link, or compile error.\n9. Treat the parent orchestrator's validation report as authoritative during repair rounds. Last-body-page fill is rendered geometric vertical occupancy computed from text and graphics bounds, not character count or word density. Do not claim that page validation passed using a character-count proxy. If the canonical validator is unavailable in the agent workspace, make the targeted repair and return control so the parent can compile and revalidate it.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
