{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"ls -ld /tmp/paper-analysis /opt/venv* /workspace/.venv* /home/agent-home/* 2>/dev/null; env | rg 'VENV|VIRTUAL|PYTHON|TMPDIR'; find /tmp /opt /home/agent-home -maxdepth 5 -name pyvenv.cfg 2>/dev/null; sed -n '800,822p' source_evidence/task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '52,76p' REPRODUCIBILITY.md; head -35 .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"ls -ld /tmp/paper-analysis /opt/venv* /workspace/.venv* /home/agent-home/* 2>/dev/null; env | rg 'VENV|VIRTUAL|PYTHON|TMPDIR'; find /tmp /opt /home/agent-home -maxdepth 5 -name pyvenv.cfg 2>/dev/null; sed -n '800,822p' source_evidence/task/evaluate_final.py; sed -n '52,76p' REPRODUCIBILITY.md; head -35 .codex/skills/write-paper-standalone/scripts/validate_claims.py\"","aggregated_output":"TASK_PYTHON=/workspace/task/.venv/bin/python\nVENV_PY=/opt/autoillustrate-venv/bin/python\nPYTHON_SHA256=c2c4321961fab0fb999d66e0cecf521c2ab3994c7992873ea99e306c1094fd5a\nTMPDIR=/agent-tmp\nWRAPPER_PYTHON=python\nPYTHON_VERSION=3.12.15\n/opt/autoillustrate-venv/pyvenv.cfg\n\n    class Network(torch.nn.Module):\n        def __init__(self, hidden, multiplier):\n            super().__init__()\n            generator = torch.Generator(device=\"cpu\").manual_seed(seed)\n            first = torch.randn(97, 256, generator=generator)\n            second = torch.randn(97, 256, generator=generator)\n            output = torch.randn(256, 97, generator=generator)\n            self.first = torch.nn.Parameter(first[:, :hidden].clone() * multiplier)\n            self.second = torch.nn.Parameter(second[:, :hidden].clone() * multiplier)\n            self.hidden_bias = torch.nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(hidden))\n            self.output = torch.nn.Parameter(output[:hidden].clone() * (multiplier / math.sqrt(hidden)))\n            self.output_bias = torch.nn.Parameter(torch.zeros(97))\n\n        def forward(self, inputs):\n            hidden = self.first[inputs[:, 0]] + self.second[inputs[:, 1]] + self.hidden_bias\n            return functional.gelu(hidden) @ self.output + self.output_bias\n\n    model = Network(width, config[\"init_multiplier\"])\n    if sum(parameter.numel() for parameter in model.parameters()) != 292 * width + 97:\n        raise RuntimeError(\"architecture shape mismatch\")\n    if arm == \"initial_norm\":\n        middle = Network(128, config[\"init_multiplier\"])\n| Study overview | Orchestrator `generate-concept-figure`, strategy + manuscript |\n| Width endpoints | `scripts/build_artifacts.py`, development/final curves |\n| Fitting/generalization onsets | Same script; sustained three-checkpoint events |\n| Final coverage table | Same script, `derived/coverage_table.tex` |\n| Development summary table | Same script, `derived/development_table.tex`, displayed to two decimals |\n| Final norm/loss diagnostics | Same script, `derived/norm_loss_records.tex` |\n| Complete final table | Same script, `derived/final_records.tex` |\n\nGenerated table content is embedded in `paper.tex` to satisfy the standalone\nsupplement contract. Figures use vector PDF where available. The source registry,\nnot rounded manuscript values, is authoritative for recomputation.\n\n## Original training reproduction (not executed during writing)\n\nThe original implementation pins NumPy 2.1.3 and PyTorch 2.5.1+cpu and uses\ndeterministic CPU operations with at most two worker threads. Linux resource\nlimits and subprocess isolation are part of the supplied evaluator. To recreate\nthe workload in a compatible Linux environment:\n\n```sh\npython3 -m venv /tmp/modular-addition-training\n/tmp/modular-addition-training/bin/pip install numpy==2.1.3\n/tmp/modular-addition-training/bin/pip install torch==2.5.1+cpu \\\n  --index-url https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cpu\n/tmp/modular-addition-training/bin/python source_evidence/task/evaluate.py \\\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Validate generated claim-grounding artifacts before paper finalization.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport stat\nimport subprocess\nimport sys\nimport tempfile\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any\n\nKEY_RE = re.compile(r\"@\\w+\\{([^,]+),\")\nEVIDENCE_REF_RE = re.compile(r\"@evidence\\[\\[[^\\]]+\\]\\]\")\nTEX_INPUT_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?:input|include)(?![A-Za-z@])\\s*\"\n    r\"(?:\\{(?P<braced>[^{}]+)\\}|(?P<unbraced>[^\\s%{}]+))\"\n)\nTEX_IMPORT_COMMAND_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\(?:input|include)(?![A-Za-z@])\")\nTEX_LOCAL_SUPPORT_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?P<command>usepackage|RequirePackage|documentclass|LoadClass)\"\n    r\"(?![A-Za-z@])(?:\\s*\\[[^\\]]*\\])?\\s*\\{(?P<targets>[^{}]+)\\}\"\n)\nTEX_LOCAL_SUPPORT_COMMAND_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\(?:usepackage|RequirePackage|documentclass|LoadClass)(?![A-Za-z@])\"\n)\nDYNAMIC_TEX_IMPORT_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\csname\\s*(?:input|include)\\s*\\\\endcsname\")\nCONDITIONAL_TOKEN_RE = re.compile(r\"\\\\if[a-zA-Z@]+\\b|\\\\else\\b|\\\\fi\\b\")\nVERBATIM_ENV_RE = re.compile(\n    r\"\\\\begin\\s*\\{(?P<env>verbatim\\*?|lstlisting|minted)\\}.*?\"\n    r\"\\\\end\\s*\\{(?P=env)\\}\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
